## 3 · Typography
| Role | Family | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Display / hook | **Space Grotesk** 600/700 | centred big statements; `-0.01em` |
| Body / sub | **Inter** 400/500 | explanatory text, captions |
| Chrome / labels / data | **IBM Plex Mono** 400/500 | section labels, source chips, tile tags |

(The serif-display option, Fraunces, remains dropped — the geometric sans hook tested strongest. Reversible at low cost as a deliberate exception.)

### Type scale — **STAGE PX on the 1920×1080 canvas · floor 20px (v0.5)**
> **Datashow talk in a difficult-light room. Every word legible from the back row. NO small text — chrome, labels, captions, tags included.** Sizes are **stage px on the fixed 1920×1080 canvas** (NOT `vw`/`clamp`): Reveal scales the whole stage as one unit, so stage-px proportions survive the scale transform and the floor stays honest on a small projector. Floor raised to **20px** by on-screen eye-test in the actual room.

| Token | Stage px | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--t-hook` | 90 | opening hook |
| `--t-h2` | 64 | section-opener headline |
| `--t-h3` | 40 | agenda section titles, sub-headers |
| `--t-sub` | 28 | sub / body / explanatory text |
| `--t-kicker` | 24 | eyebrow / thematic label (mono) |
| `--t-chrome` | 22 | nav, section label, slider (mono) |
| `--t-caption` | 20 | captions, chips, tile tags (mono) — **FLOOR: the smallest text allowed anywhere** |

**Legibility floor rule:** `--t-caption` (20px stage) is the smallest text permitted on any slide. Nothing — no footnote, tag, chip, or source line — goes below it. If content forces text below the floor, the content is too dense: cut it or split the slide. (`--t-micro` deleted; it was sub-floor. `clamp()`/`vw` removed entirely — stage px only, per the Reveal scale-transform fix.)

**Full-frame rule:** use the whole slide. Margins are breathing room, not waste — headlines and key visuals occupy the frame confidently. Bigger is safer in this room.

Mono chrome: `.16–.32em` uppercase. Display: `-0.01em`. Body: normal.

